Z||000000||blazin'||11-02-2001||11:02 PM||||Can someone give me the dimensions of the sub box for the fiero? I plan on making one for behind the passenger seat. What size sub can it hold? I don't think it could hold too big of one as the magnets on them can get  quite large! I'm also considering a box for the front compartment.....But I'm gonna think about it first! Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroPerformance||11-02-2001||11:56 PM||||I built mine to go in the passenger foot well. It fits nicely and leaves enough foot room. The front of the box (taken off for the picture) doubles as a foot rest.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mybox1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mybox2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mybox3.jpg"> <P>I have an 8" Rockford Fosgate DVC HX2 in there. I still don't have an amp so I haven't had a chance to hear it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> All of my money is tied up in the engine rebuild.<P>Hope this helps you.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||blazin'||11-03-2001||12:09 AM||||Great!!!! I've seen that type before! Would you mind giving me the specs for that? It looks to be a cheap and simple project! Is there anyway a bigger sub can fit?<BR>I have a bass cannon that's also 8 inches in my truck. It doesn't sound too bad, but it's old and I only paid 20 bucks for it!! lol||||reg||1
